# Real-time audio

Inside `processBlock`, `process()`, or `renderNextBlock`:

- No `new`, `delete`, `malloc`, `std::vector` growth, `std::string`, or `setSize` that can reallocate.
- No mutexes, critical sections, file I/O, logging, or network.
- Size every buffer in `prepare` / `prepareToPlay`. Chunk later calls to that capacity.
- Smooth continuous parameters with `juce::SmoothedValue` or a one-pole. Do not read a raw APVTS value per sample.
- Put `juce::ScopedNoDenormals` at the start of the audio function.
- On a drum trigger, reset oscillator phase to 0 unless the request asks for free-running drift.

```cpp
// Bad: allocates if the host block grows
scratch.setSize(1, numSamples);
// Good: scratch was sized to the prepare() maximum
jassert(numSamples <= scratch.getNumSamples());
```
